# Build context for `gcloud run deploy --source .`
#
# The working tree is ~3.5 GB (2 GB of raw logger exports, an 879 MB venv,
# 399 MB of generated artifacts). None of it belongs in the image, and all of it
# would otherwise be uploaded to Cloud Build on every deploy.
#
# Allow-list, not deny-list: ignore everything, then re-admit only what the
# container needs. A new data folder dropped in the repo is then excluded by
# default rather than silently shipped.
#
# NOTE: gcloud uses this file INSTEAD of .gitignore once it exists.

# 1. Ignore everything ...
*

# 2. ... but keep descending into directories so the rules below can match.
!*/

# 3. Re-admit exactly what the Dockerfile needs.
!/Dockerfile
!/requirements.txt
!/backend/**
!/frontend/**

# 4. Re-exclude heavy or irrelevant paths inside the admitted trees.
#    (Later rules win, so these override the negations above.)
backend/venv/
backend/*.pdf
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# 5. Belt-and-braces: never walk these at all.
.git/
/artifacts/
/uploads/
/logs/
/tools/
/data/
/reports/
/docs/
/tests/
.vercel/
.vscode/

# 6. Data and report files, wherever they appear.
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.csv
*.wlg
*.parquet
*.docx
*.pdf
*.png
